section.p:
  A z-score is a value that measures how far away a data item within a data set is from the mean, measured in standard deviations. The formula for calculating the z-score of a data item x is:
  z=\frac{x-\mu}{\sigma}
Where \mu is the mean of a data set, and \sigma is the standard deviation. A sample mean and sample standard deviation may be used in place of the population values.
